<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · river</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kabompo River</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Kabompo is a river of north-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zambia">Zambia</a>, a major tributary of the upper <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zambezi">Zambezi</a>. It rises near the watershed with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/congo-basin">Congo basin</a> and flows south-west through woodland to join the Zambezi. Its headwaters were settled from the 18th century by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lunda-empire">Lunda</a> groups, including the Ndembu chiefdom of Kanongesha.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/kabompo-river.jpg" alt="Kabompo River" width="320" height="320" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: MarkTownsendZambia · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kabompo_River.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
